fd-a054-8baee9c84dc6" :question/math-academy-id "q-288058" :question/problem "Which of the following equations has no solutions?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $4x - 2 = 4x + 3$\n- **II.** $3x + 4 = 3x + 4$\n- **III.** $5x = 2x + 6$" :question/worked-solution "The equations reduce respectively to -2=3, an identity, and x=2. Only the first has no solutions."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297172 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "533b9094-d677-5376-88f4-8f426a2a4cf6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438046} {:answer/id #uuid "2b5a3d38-5a54-5a47-a0a8-64956fa7cdee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438047}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2b5a3d38-5a54-5a47-a0a8-64956fa7cdee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438047} :answer-field/id #uuid "bd3eb9cd-0eda-53a6-bbc3-9f6bfbd15e06" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439052} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "38767ef4-49fe-519a-b838-3b77b5b7521b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438048} {:answer/id #uuid "36138474-e8c9-5d26-acfa-e3b7ef2f057d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438049}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "36138474-e8c9-5d26-acfa-e3b7ef2f057d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438049} :answer-field/id #uuid "e6d2fdbb-10bc-55e5-8c2c-6df645004975" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439053} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4435d623-199a-5d01-8347-ab72dc2191c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438050} {:answer/id #uuid "83476a1a-ee79-50fd-b7a1-580c8914eb50" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438051}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4435d623-199a-5d01-8347-ab72dc2191c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438050} :answer-field/id #uuid "5259194c-9195-582d-b7ec-c468a67fa9be" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439054}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1b892079-10a1-5d68-a34f-01695fac566e" :question/math-academy-id "q-288066" :question/problem "Which of the following equations has no solutions?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $-3u+4=-3u-1$\n- **II.** $2u+5=2u+8$\n- **III.** $6u-2=3u+1$" :question/worked-solution "Let's attempt to solve each equation in turn:\n\n- For the first equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3u+4 & =-3u-1 \\\\ -3u+4+3u & =-3u-1+3u \\\\ 4 & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is false for all values of $u.$ Therefore, the equation $-3u+4=-3u-1$ has no solutions.\n\n- For the second equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2u+5 & =2u+8 \\\\ 2u+5-2u & =2u+8-2u \\\\ 5 & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is false for all values of $u.$ Therefore, the equation $2u+5=2u+8$ has no solutions.\n\n- For the third equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6u-2 & =3u+1 \\\\ 6u-2-3u+2 & =3u+1-3u+2 \\\\ 3u & =3 \\\\ u & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation $6u-2=3u+1$ has the unique solution $u=1.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297173 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5bbb7117-6145-53ca-ad4c-bad31bb9f9af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438052} {:answer/id #uuid "671b6a92-35b3-597e-be0a-c9cb5b791a09" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438053}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "671b6a92-35b3-597e-be0a-c9cb5b791a09" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438053} :answer-field/id #uuid "27b44160-5603-5c9b-a638-902e6099883a" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439055} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4222c763-212d-511f-8fbd-f58190e2e759" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438054} {:answer/id #uuid "3f98701c-3dbf-5adb-90ef-8da0bf27f04a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438055}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3f98701c-3dbf-5adb-90ef-8da0bf27f04a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438055} :answer-field/id #uuid "0b686279-275d-59b3-9845-affb7909a340" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439056} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b38af36b-5c28-52cd-827f-5d2c79c4e02b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438056} {:answer/id #uuid "5c014ef5-df66-55a4-9f0c-a5b36748f66b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438057}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b38af36b-5c28-52cd-827f-5d2c79c4e02b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438056} :answer-field/id #uuid "61cc02af-d6dd-57ac-bd35-0666f970edb9" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439057}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9e1fdbd8-4927-548c-aafb-62f0ed007aa2" :question/math-academy-id "q-288070" :question/problem "Which of the following equations has no solutions?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $-4y+2=-4y-5$\n- **II.** $6y+3=6y-1$\n- **III.** $5y-7=2y+1$" :question/worked-solution "Let's attempt to solve each equation in turn:\n\n- For the first equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4y+2 & =-4y-5 \\\\ -4y+2+4y & =-4y-5+4y \\\\ 2 & =-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is false for all values of $y.$ Therefore, the equation $-4y+2=-4y-5$ has no solutions.\n\n- For the second equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6y+3 & =6y-1 \\\\ 6y+3-6y & =6y-1-6y \\\\ 3 & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is false for all values of $y.$ Therefore, the equation $6y+3=6y-1$ has no solutions.\n\n- For the third equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5y-7 & =2y+1 \\\\ 5y-7-2y+7 & =2y+1-2y+7 \\\\ 3y & =8 \\\\ y & =\\frac{8}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation $5y-7=2y+1$ has the unique solution $y=\\frac{8}{3}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297174 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b7fde21a-0d8d-594b-a745-db65189df67f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438058} {:answer/id #uuid "8ece53fa-2eb2-5b1c-b285-9b87f8f4daae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438059}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8ece53fa-2eb2-5b1c-b285-9b87f8f4daae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438059} :answer-field/id #uuid "84307fe1-029d-5028-aa23-639aad6faaed" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439058} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0d5cc2ff-b49f-5c4a-970f-cdbb15792abc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438060} {:answer/id #uuid "e7c10c6b-8ee7-5fa9-9d42-6f7cf79b8350" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438061}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0d5cc2ff-b49f-5c4a-970f-cdbb15792abc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438060} :answer-field/id #uuid "5867c7b6-4f6f-5a06-af87-9049cb497b9a" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439059} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ee6986a4-2a71-509d-9e9c-688693540c97" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438062} {:answer/id #uuid "d69e090d-5eb5-5b4e-b8b4-4433ad55707e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438063}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ee6986a4-2a71-509d-9e9c-688693540c97" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438062} :answer-field/id #uuid "5782e1ec-cdc2-5bee-a672-c727cc727606" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439060}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "22403a37-d9b4-5866-bee2-a28d9c27c3b3" :question/math-academy-id "q-288072" :question/problem "Which of the following equations has no solutions?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $2z-4=2z+1$\n- **II.** $5z+6=5z+6$\n- **III.** $3z+2=z+4$" :question/worked-solution "Let's attempt to solve each equation in turn:\n\n- For the first equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2z-4 & =2z+1 \\\\ 2z-4-2z & =2z+1-2z \\\\ -4 & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is false for all values of $z.$ Therefore, the equation $2z-4=2z+1$ has no solutions.\n\n- For the second equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5z+6 & =5z+6 \\\\ 5z+6-5z & =5z+6-5z \\\\ 6 & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is true for all values of $z.$\n\n- For the third equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3z+2 & =z+4 \\\\ 3z+2-z-2 & =z+4-z-2 \\\\ 2z & =2 \\\\ z & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation $3z+2=z+4$ has the unique solution $z=1.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297175 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "220ca104-2317-5355-b6f9-238d7b5e2da7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438064} {:answer/id #uuid "29bf254a-4e1b-5c2b-b3eb-48992ead8349" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438065}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "220ca104-2317-5355-b6f9-238d7b5e2da7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438064} :answer-field/id #uuid "ad481161-f390-54f8-b99c-f0b018cbf93d" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439061} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7b8b1efb-e712-53d2-a457-f8729510edfa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438066} {:answer/id #uuid "2a584f47-36b5-5f9e-a333-07b07506ccab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438067}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7b8b1efb-e712-53d2-a457-f8729510edfa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438066} :answer-field/id #uuid "20ba482c-6e9d-5a6e-a9d8-c815e493f55e" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439062} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8617b3bd-b969-56d6-b993-a80ccaf50cf4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438068} {:answer/id #uuid "5f78f8cc-2978-55d1-9b15-8c6c21d6c9be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438069}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5f78f8cc-2978-55d1-9b15-8c6c21d6c9be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438069} :answer-field/id #uuid "e00e8280-0c1c-5114-85aa-6e63beddc409" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439063}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ae9bca83-e68f-5756-9519-1447b4343c01" :question/math-academy-id "q-288073" :question/problem "Which of the following equations has no solutions?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $3w+2=2w+2$\n- **II.** $4w-7=4w-7$\n- **III.** $6w+5=6w+9$" :question/worked-solution "Let's attempt to solve each equation in turn:\n\n- For the first equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3w+2 & =2w+2 \\\\ 3w+2-2w-2 & =2w+2-2w-2 \\\\ w & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation $3w+2=2w+2$ has the unique solution $w=0.$\n\n- For the second equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4w-7 & =4w-7 \\\\ 4w-7-4w & =4w-7-4w \\\\ -7 & =-7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is true for all values of $w.$\n\n- For the third equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6w+5 & =6w+9 \\\\ 6w+5-6w & =6w+9-6w \\\\ 5 & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is false for all values of $w.$ Therefore, the equation $6w+5=6w+9$ has no solutions.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297176 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "011e4d4e-2435-5fb2-8574-19c1dbaf09f3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438070} {:answer/id #uuid "8f578d76-5649-5082-be77-dd1b0e5dcbac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438071}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "011e4d4e-2435-5fb2-8574-19c1dbaf09f3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438070} :answer-field/id #uuid "94fbe475-e14d-5369-a8f5-50ea65227255" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439064} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cb87e3b1-181c-58b9-a433-5f220bb4a2af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438072} {:answer/id #uuid "d8bb8bbe-2133-551e-8af1-914f9e44ca08" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438073}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d8bb8bbe-2133-551e-8af1-914f9e44ca08" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438073} :answer-field/id #uuid "29f521f2-17c5-5d89-845f-2032ff8443ed" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439065} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "39b56f35-4411-58e8-91b8-70740004bb8a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438074} {:answer/id #uuid "855857a7-7338-5129-b4f4-752ae0f7d9dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438075}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "39b56f35-4411-58e8-91b8-70740004bb8a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438074} :answer-field/id #uuid "345c1cd0-794d-566a-9e4b-9b18bedff524" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439066}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6480ee2c-c900-5448-85b3-32f94538971e" :question/math-academy-id "q-288074" :question/problem "Which of the following equations has no solutions?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $9v-5=4v+2$\n- **II.** $2v+3=2v+7$\n- **III.** $5v-1=5v-1$" :question/worked-solution "Let's attempt to solve each equation in turn:\n\n- For the first equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9v-5 & =4v+2 \\\\ 9v-5-4v+5 & =4v+2-4v+5 \\\\ 5v & =7 \\\\ v & =\\frac{7}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation $9v-5=4v+2$ has the unique solution $v=\\frac{7}{5}.$\n\n- For the second equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2v+3 & =2v+7 \\\\ 2v+3-2v & =2v+7-2v \\\\ 3 & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is false for all values of $v.$ Therefore, the equation $2v+3=2v+7$ has no solutions.\n\n- For the third equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5v-1 & =5v-1 \\\\ 5v-1-5v & =5v-1-5v \\\\ -1 & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is true for all values of $v.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508100 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c78cb3d-2cc5-5e2c-9e55-a80e139339bf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507616} {:answer/id #uuid "306bd0fa-00bf-5a91-966b-275a7a3521a4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507663} {:answer/id #uuid "750f8f74-e77a-5d2e-8f3d-ca74279509fa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507769} {:answer/id #uuid "b5b51887-d353-59f8-948b-51c3d03accf9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507848} {:answer/id #uuid "b8fb200b-60c0-5f70-ae27-f8dd1334ced2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507854}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0c78cb3d-2cc5-5e2c-9e55-a80e139339bf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507616} :answer-field/id #uuid "4dd41eb7-fc07-5b0d-8a34-e949bc172ef0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507976}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d0bffce7-58da-5042-ae7f-fb5de551e1a7" :question/math-academy-id "q-288069" :question/problem "Which of the following equations has no solutions?\n\nI. $2x-3=2x+4$\n\nII. $-5x+7=-2x-2$\n\nIII. $4x+1=4x+1$" :question/worked-solution "Let's attempt to solve each equation in turn:\n\n- For the first equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x-3 & =2x+4 \\\\ 2x-3-2x & =2x+4-2x \\\\ -3 & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is false for all values of $x.$ Therefore, the equation $2x-3=2x+4$ has no solutions.\n\n- For the second equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-5x+7 & =-2x-2 \\\\ -5x+7+2x-7 & =-2x-2+2x-7 \\\\ -3x & =-9 \\\\ x & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation $-5x+7=-2x-2$ has the unique solution $x=3.$\n\n- For the third equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x+1 & =4x+1 \\\\ 4x+1-4x & =4x+1-4x \\\\ 1 & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is true for all values of $x.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] :knowledge-point/title "Identifying an Equation With No Solutions"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204090 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186203853 :question/id #uuid "cba9196c-fdc3-594d-a1ad-948cf75bd366" :question/math-academy-id "e-17213" :question/problem "Consider the equation in the variable $y,$ given by\n\n$$\n4(r - 2)y = -8\n$$\n\nwhere $r$ is a constant. Given that this equation has no solution, what is the value of $r?$" :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have an equation of the form\n\n$$\nax = b\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are constants, and $b\\neq 0.$ If $a = 0,$ then the equation has no solution.\n\nNotice that this equation is in the form $ay = b.$ In this case, \n\n$$\na = 4(r - 2), \\qquad b = -8.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation has no solution if\n\n$$\n4(r - 2) = 0.\n$$\n\nSolving this for $r,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4(r-2) & =0 \\\\ \\frac{4(r-2)}{4} & =\\frac{0}{4} \\\\ r-2 & =0 \\\\ r & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c0e7426e-553d-5f20-811f-15f3a5ea0056" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204596 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8639ce62-5e23-5361-b682-c7000582d54e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186203491} {:answer/id #uuid "f6b1d5cd-7280-5a3b-b538-d976044c6e94" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186203492} {:answer/id #uuid "fcfa0123-90e9-5186-b54d-3ae7859972b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186203493} {:answer/id #uuid "3cb6287c-2e23-513c-b813-c514eaaaaae3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186203494} {:answer/id #uuid "7dffe079-6e58-5eee-a2d4-f50f9c6c606c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186203495}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8639ce62-5e23-5361-b682-c7000582d54e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186203491} :answer-field/id #uuid "b9422b9e-c65d-596a-90ac-20fde363b97c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186203490}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b6c453dd-3b6b-5f65-bf37-1fc261d1f26a" :question/math-academy-id "q-287665" :question/problem "Consider the equation in the variable $x,$ given by\n\n$$\n2px=3\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is a constant. Given that this equation has no solution, what is the value of $p?$" :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have an equation of the form\n\n$$\nax=b\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are constants, and $b\\ne 0.$ If $a=0,$ then the equation has no solution.\n\nNotice that this equation is in the form $ax=b.$ In this case, \n\n$$\na=2p,\\,b=3.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation has no solution if\n\n$$\n2p=0.\n$$\n\nSolving this for $p,$ we get\n\n$$\np=0.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204602 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1ab2ed61-9a09-5b11-8a3a-164d58ee2841" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295425} {:answer/id #uuid "3661811c-5e94-5d73-b96b-461bf4e8e913" :