wer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507713} {:answer/id #uuid "9bd678d9-2685-5d26-b56a-e4126c2c4ff5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507816} {:answer/id #uuid "a039287f-5135-5191-970c-859892a6a41c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507823} {:answer/id #uuid "b5a20a9e-5f1a-5668-bd6f-c5fd978a900f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507847}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9bd678d9-2685-5d26-b56a-e4126c2c4ff5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507816} :answer-field/id #uuid "fa2138e2-b337-52b3-8a3d-5fd1ad2f1eba" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508031}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6feec1bb-9d5b-5e0f-99d7-930f0577f85b" :question/math-academy-id "q-288107" :question/problem "Consider the equation in the variable $t,$ given by\n\n$$\n5qt=-4\n$$\n\nwhere $q$ is a constant. Given that this equation has no solution, what is the value of $q?$" :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have an equation of the form\n\n$$\nax=b\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are constants, and $b\\ne 0.$ If $a=0,$ then the equation has no solution.\n\nNotice that this equation is in the form $at=b.$ In this case,\n\n$$\na=5q,\\,b=-4.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation has no solution if\n\n$$\n5q=0.\n$$\n\nSolving this for $q,$ we get\n\n$$\nq=0.\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Solving For an Unknown Parameter"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204091 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186203878 :question/id #uuid "5ee14499-89b0-59a3-9f13-b0a00c0e518d" :question/math-academy-id "e-18853" :question/problem "Consider the equation in the variable $z,$ given by\n\n$$\n(r - 9)z + 2 = -1\n$$\n\nwhere $r$ is a constant. Given that this equation has no solution, what is the value of $r?$" :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have an equation of the form\n\n$$\nax = b\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are constants, and $b\\neq 0.$ If $a = 0,$ then the equation has no solution.\n\nFirst, let's write our equation in the form $az = b{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-9)z+2 & =-1 \\\\ (r-9)z+2-2 & =-1-2 \\\\ {{(r-9)}_{⏟}}_{a}z & ={{-3}_{⏟}}_{b}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation has no solution if\n\n$$\nr - 9 = 0.\n$$\n\nSolving this for $r,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r-9 & =0 \\\\ r & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ba644b27-7245-5b7b-8cd6-2493836a7d03" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204597 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c2937687-dedd-5964-bb4d-22153fc13d86" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296297}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c2937687-dedd-5964-bb4d-22153fc13d86" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296297} :answer-field/id #uuid "4a06a891-d4f2-506a-bdd0-0692d7f6be31" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296775}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "38670cb7-04d7-5bd3-bbc0-32b596369870" :question/math-academy-id "q-287667" :question/problem "Consider the equation in the variable $x,$ given by\n\n$$\n2(p-4)x+2=5\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is a constant. Given that this equation has no solution, what is the value of $p?$\n\n$p=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have an equation of the form\n\n$$\nax=b\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are constants, and $b\\ne 0.$ If $a=0,$ then the equation has no solution.\n\nFirst, let's write our equation in the form $ax=b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(p-4)x+2 & =5 \\\\ 2(p-4)x+2-2 & =5-2 \\\\ {{2(p-4)}_{⏟}}_{a}x & ={{3}_{⏟}}_{b}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation has no solution if\n\n$$\n2(p-4)=0.\n$$\n\nSolving this for $p,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(p-4) & =0 \\\\ \\frac{2(p-4)}{2} & =\\frac{0}{2} \\\\ p-4 & =0 \\\\ p & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204603 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/id #uuid "88983c17-8c0d-5f28-8a83-c178d5d425cd" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186203522}] :question/id #uuid "eafa17e2-08f9-58c7-8e3f-be7946a2edcf" :question/math-academy-id "q-288643" :question/problem "Consider the equation in the variable $z$, given by\n$(r + 3)z + 5 =-4$\nwhere $r$ is a constant. Given that this equation has no solution, what is the value of $r$?$r =$\n{{field-1}}"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297201 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9611e30a-239c-5cbf-b771-57108c2e379b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296065}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9611e30a-239c-5cbf-b771-57108c2e379b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296065} :answer-field/id #uuid "28c6d002-88fb-5a97-a562-15802c967ffc" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296712}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d326f3de-7c8d-596a-800c-00170de0cabb" :question/math-academy-id "q-288634" :question/problem "Consider the equation in the variable $x,$ given by\n\n$$\n3(p+2)x+7=10\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is a constant. Given that this equation has no solution, what is the value of $p?$\n\n$p=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have an equation of the form\n\n$$\nax=b\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are constants, and $b\\ne 0.$ If $a=0,$ then the equation has no solution.\n\nFirst, let's write our equation in the form $ax=b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3(p+2)x+7 & =10 \\\\ 3(p+2)x+7-7 & =10-7 \\\\ {{3(p+2)}_{⏟}}_{a}x & ={{3}_{⏟}}_{b}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation has no solution if\n\n$$\n3(p+2)=0.\n$$\n\nSolving this for $p,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3(p+2) & =0 \\\\ \\frac{3(p+2)}{3} & =\\frac{0}{3} \\\\ p+2 & =0 \\\\ p & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297202 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "488785de-3552-5c44-b37c-f80db84151a3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295682}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "488785de-3552-5c44-b37c-f80db84151a3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295682} :answer-field/id #uuid "4f518425-6bb3-513e-9a2f-cd6d4cd2d157" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296784}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e9e21b0c-1002-52c2-8ff0-0958a8c28640" :question/math-academy-id "q-288644" :question/problem "Consider the equation in the variable $v,$ given by\n\n$$\n(k-2)v-3=5\n$$\n\nwhere $k$ is a constant. Given that this equation has no solution, what is the value of $k?$\n\n$k=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have an equation of the form\n\n$$\nax=b\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are constants, and $b\\ne 0.$ If $a=0,$ then the equation has no solution.\n\nFirst, let's write our equation in the form $av=b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(k-2)v-3 & =5 \\\\ (k-2)v-3+3 & =5+3 \\\\ {{(k-2)}_{⏟}}_{a}v & ={{8}_{⏟}}_{b}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation has no solution if\n\n$$\nk-2=0.\n$$\n\nSolving this for $k,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}k-2 & =0 \\\\ k & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297203 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1b250822-5029-5ba9-b12a-849c9b646e53" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295427}] :answer-field/correct {:an